# gen_fu_l56_storm_vacuity_companion.log -- the storm-regime vacuity is NOT closed by landing 54 (TB Infra,
# 2026-09-05). Companion to gen_fu_l52_commands_corrigendum.log, whose bytes are untouched
# (md5 44ed232180fc5db85d8f7403c8d6a26e, 7506 bytes), answering rev60's Medium and the Critic's M-3.
#
# THE SENTENCE THIS CORRECTS. gen_fu_l52_commands_corrigendum.log:57 reads
#   "This is the block the DV Lead later ruled VACUOUS rather than less sensitive
#    (gen_fu_l52_vacuity_corrigendum.log), and landing 54 removes the shape that caused it."
# The second clause is false. Landing 54 does not remove that shape.
#
# WHY, from the committed source rather than from the review. At b9e5fad, gen_checkers_pkg.sv:118 is
#   if (expects[i].lines[17:0] != 0 || expects[i].nmi) begin expects[i].order_at = st.order; expects[i].unmasked = 0; keep.push_back(expects[i]); end
# That runs on EVERY interrupt entry, and it zeroes the accrued takeable count of every expectation that
# survives the entry, not only of the one the entry satisfied. Under a storm the entries are back to back, so
# the count is reset before it can reach the bound, and a withheld line outranked by the lines actually being
# taken is never judged. Accrual changed how the count survives a MASKED record; it did not change how the
# count survives an ENTRY, and the storm vacuity is the second of those.
# (The line has since moved to :114 in my working tree, where removing the NMI nesting counter shortened the
# file. The text above is what is committed at b9e5fad and is what the sentence was written about.)
#
# WHAT LANDING 54 DID CLOSE, so the correction does not overshoot. The SOFTWARE-TOGGLE vacuity: a line raised,
# some records in which it could have been taken, a software clear of mstatus.MIE, more records, a software
# set, and then more takeable records. Before landing 54 the masked stretch discarded everything spent before
# it, so the bound could never expire however long the line waited; after it the spent records are kept and
# the case is judged. That is measured in gen_fu_l54_irq_nmi_mask_accrual.log, whose red on that shape reads
# forty-two records elapsed against eighteen takeable. It is a different vacuity from the storm one.
#
# THE MEASUREMENT THAT SETTLES IT IS THE CRITIC'S AND IS ATTRIBUTED, NOT ADOPTED. On its own compiles it ran
# the l52 storm fixture with the external line withheld against the FIXED checker and read zero fires with the
# ablation also zero, both runs ending at the alive timeout, while the same mutation fires twelve times on the
# NMI storm smoke. So the storm arm's zero is a property of that fixture rather than of the storm regime, and
# the fixed checker still catches a withheld line on a storm smoke that gives it an unmasked stretch. I have
# not reproduced the twelve and this companion does not claim it; what I verified myself is the entry restart
# above, which is the mechanism the numbers are consistent with.
#
# THE CONTRADICTION WAS INSIDE ONE LANDING AND THAT IS THE PART WORTH RECORDING. gen_fu_l54_irq_nmi_mask_accrual.log
# and gen_fu_l52_commands_corrigendum.log went into the same commit, b9e5fad. The first says at :72-74 that a
# regime-independent end-of-test expectation is still owed and describes what it must reconcile. The second
# says the shape is already removed. Both were written by me on the same day and neither read the other. A
# corrigendum is exactly the artefact a reader trusts to be careful, and I wrote a claim into one that the
# landing's own evidence log contradicts four files away.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY CLOSES IT, stated so the sentence is not merely withdrawn. The regime-independent end-of-test
# expectation: every raised, enabled line reconciled at the END OF TEST rather than by another per-record
# bound, since a per-record bound is what goes vacuous under load. Its NMI term is NMI mode and debug mode
# only, never mstatus.MIE, because the NMI has no enable bit and rtl/ibex_controller.sv:498 ORs irq_nm outside
# irq_enabled. The DV Lead's form already carries the vacuity as open and closing only by that reconciliation,
# so the plan and this record now agree.
